Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 22:22:13 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 253/258] feat(execution): report schema v3 embeds provider
 manifest and resolution decision

Bump REPORT_SCHEMA_VERSION 2 -> 3 and make the execution report
self-contained for manifest-backed facts:

* provider_manifest carries the invoked provider's canonical
  ProviderCapability.to_dict() document, its recomputed canonical digest and
  the capability snapshot digest;
* resolution_decision carries the declared/selected resolution decision
  frozen in the plan plus its recomputed canonical digest;
* provider_identity.py anchors the embedded invoked manifest and the declared
  decision to registered code/registry constants (portable manifest rebuilt
  from the OpDefinition registry; AOCL sha256 / BLIS tag+commit / arch / ABI
  widths / build options / symbol lists / pack / artifact kind / versions /
  recomputed provider_artifact_digest), so rewriting every report copy
  including the embedded documents and their digests is still refused;
* every manifest-backed declaration copy is reconciled against the embedded
  ground truth: artifact/resolved library, artifact.pack.strategy and
  included_in_timing, timing pack_semantics, numeric class, determinism,
  reduction_order/_id, implementation, provider/artifact version constants,
  vendor provider_artifact_digest and the resolution.plan_digest decision
  copy;
* guarantees.reduction_order and guarantees.deterministic now follow the
  invoked manifest (executed-path semantics), matching resolved/artifact and
  the existing reduction_order_id behaviour; all registered providers are
  deterministic so the only genuine value change is the runtime-fallback
  reduction order;
* v2 reports are rejected as legacy (report_schema_version_legacy_rejected),
  never upgraded; the embedded digest/body mismatch cases fail closed;
* the probe-free canonical builders aocl_capability_entry and
  aocl_int8_capability_entry are extracted from the capability constructors
  and shared with validation (byte-identical documents verified);
* tests: schema-v3 tamper matrix (single copy + coordinated all-copies),
  genuine portable/vendor/fallback/int8 passes, probe-free validation,
  v2 migration and digest inconsistency; docs updated in 0006 section 7.1.

Known residuals (documented): runtime/measured facts, unpinned probe facts,
coordinated resolution.plan_digest rewrite (plan payload not embedded), and
whole-registered-identity substitution.
