+**Schema v3 embedded ground truth and the registered identity anchor**:
+
+* ``provider_manifest`` must carry the invoked provider's
+  ``ProviderCapability.to_dict()`` document, its canonical digest recomputed
+  from the body, its ``provider_id`` and the capability snapshot digest;
+  ``resolution_decision`` must carry the canonical declared-selection
+  document (selected provider/version/implementation/numeric class/
+  determinism/reduction-order ids/library plus the plan artifact facts) and
+  its recomputed canonical digest;
+* the embedded invoked manifest is reconstructed from code/registry constants
+  by :mod:`pypto.execution.provider_identity` and must match exactly:
+  provider id, version, implementation, numeric class, determinism, reduction
+  order, pack strategy/inclusion, artifact kind, dtypes/rank/stride/preconditions,
+  contract digests, thread model, and -- for AOCL -- the pinned sha256,
+  BLIS tag/commit, arch id/string, ABI widths, build options, symbol lists
+  and the recomputed ``provider_artifact_digest``.  The portable manifest is
+  rebuilt from the ``OpDefinition`` registry;
+* the decision's ``selected_*``/``artifact_*`` manifest facts are reconciled
+  against the registered identity of the declared provider; without a runtime
+  fallback they must also equal the embedded invoked manifest, including the
+  probe-variable library fields;
+* every report copy of an invoked-manifest-backed fact is reconciled against
+  the embedded document: ``resolved.{provider,provider_version,
+  implementation,library,numeric_class}``, ``artifact.{kind,provider_version,
+  library,pack.strategy,pack.included_in_timing,provider_artifact_digest}``,
+  the registered lowering/runner/wire/abi version constants,
+  ``guarantees.{numeric_class,precision_class,deterministic,
+  reduction_order,reduction_order_id}`` and
+  ``timing.timing_basis.pack_semantics``;
+* ``resolution.plan_digest`` is reconciled against the decision document
+  copy.
+
 **What is an explanation layer, not normative** (no in-document ground truth
 is enforced for the payloads below): positional
 ``resolution.candidates[*].checks[*]`` payloads
@@ -70,34 +105,41 @@ the declared/invoked candidates; ``stride_class``/``deterministic`` only for
 the selected candidate), and
 ``resolution.rejections[*].failed_checks[*].detail`` payloads;
 ``resolution.why``; coverage counts/flags/``parent_opcode``;
-``dispatch.*_reconciled`` flags; ``gates.*``; free-text
-``timing.timing_basis.*``; ``rejections[*].library_version``/``message``;
-``artifact.content_digest``; ``resolution.plan_digest``; ``thread_state.
-loaded_threads``; non-selected providers' ``deterministic``; the per-event
-``fallback_events[*]`` payloads (the list itself and
-``resolution.degraded`` are reconciled); ``tie_break_key`` prefixes (only its
-terminal candidate id is anchored); ``resources.parallelism`` knobs
-(``worker_count``, ``oversubscription_policy``, ``cpu_affinity``) and the
-thread-environment accounting surfaced in ``thread_state``; and the
-manifest-only *value-vs-external-truth* facts (vendor implementation
-ids/provider artifact digests/artifact versions,
-``guarantees.reduction_order``/``reduction_order_id``, and the selected
-provider's exact resolved thread mode when it was not invoked).
-
-Even where the value-vs-manifest part is a boundary, the **in-document pairs
-are enforced**: ``artifact.pack.strategy`` must equal
-``timing.timing_basis.pack_semantics`` (``report_pack_semantics_mismatch``),
-and ``artifact.library`` must equal ``resolved.library``
-(``report_artifact_library_not_reconciled``).  Only comparing those values
-against the provider's external manifest is out of scope for
-``validate_report_schema``.
-
-**Irreducible single-document limit**: a forger who rewrites *every* copy of
-a fact that has no external truth in the document (request dtype/shape,
-capability features, manifest-only facts) can still produce a self-consistent
-report.  Platform features and provider manifests are not embedded, so
-``validate_report_schema`` cannot act as an execution authorization.
-``validate_report_schema`` runs in ``ExecutionReport.__init__`` **after**
+``dispatch.*_reconciled`` flags; ``gates.*``; the free-text
+``timing.timing_basis`` strings (``pack_semantics`` is now normative);
+``rejections[*].library_version``/``message``; ``artifact.content_digest``;
+``thread_state.loaded_threads``; non-selected providers' candidate
+``deterministic``/``numeric_class``/``provider_version`` echoes (their
+manifests are not embedded); the per-event ``fallback_events[*]`` payloads
+(the list itself and ``resolution.degraded`` are reconciled);
+``tie_break_key`` prefixes (only its terminal candidate id is anchored);
+``resources.parallelism`` knobs (``worker_count``, ``oversubscription_policy``,
+``cpu_affinity``) and the thread-environment accounting surfaced in
+``thread_state``.
+
+**Residual boundaries** (a single report cannot self-certify these; they are
+registered in ``docs/10-architecture/0006-...`` section 7.1 and the
+schema-v3 brief):
+
+* runtime/measured facts: ``timing.*`` numbers, ``artifact.content_digest``,
+  the concrete ``dispatch.threads_used`` value (only its cross-copies are
+  reconciled), coverage counts, ``gates.*`` and resource accounting;
+* probe facts that are not pinned by code: host capability
+  ``features``/target snapshot digest, and the non-pinned AOCL fingerprint
+  fields (``path``/``name``/``size_bytes``/``default_threads``/BLIS version
+  suffix);
+* ``resolution.plan_digest``: the plan payload is not embedded, so the
+  decision digest is not the plan-digest preimage; a coordinated rewrite of
+  ``resolution.plan_digest`` + the decision body + the recomputed decision
+  digest is accepted (the single-copy and non-repaired forms are refused);
+* registered-identity substitution: the anchor proves that the embedded
+  document is one of the *registered* canonical provider manifests, not that
+  this identity actually ran.  A wholly coherent report (all copies, both
+  embedded documents and both digests) for a different registered provider
+  can still be constructed.
+
+Because of those residuals, ``validate_report_schema`` is **not** an
+execution authorization.  It runs in ``ExecutionReport.__init__`` **after**
 execution; no execution path consumes a report, and a downstream consumer
 must not re-plan from a report.  Execution authorization remains
 ``execute_matmul_plan`` -> :func:`pypto.execution.entry._verify_plan_binding`,
@@ -105,7 +147,7 @@ which re-runs the resolver against the digest-checked capability snapshot.
 
 The boundary list is mirrored in
 ``docs/10-architecture/0006-...`` section 7.1 and
-``_meta/pypto-x/view-mode-require/brief.zh-CN.md`` sections 14-15.
+``_meta/pypto-x/report-schema-v2/brief.zh-CN.md``.
